  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115662",
      "title": "Introducing the Component Lifecycle: ngOnInit",
      "lectureOrder": 123,
      "videoOrder": 117,
      "sourceHash": "071e1259d6b57420a0592e09a1238ec2363604f233619cd33618788f6ee972aa",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 2.856,
          "en": "Here I am using the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.856,
          "end": 5.19,
          "en": "of this component class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.19,
          "end": 9.03,
          "en": "to set up an interval whenever this class is instantiated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.03,
          "end": 12.693,
          "en": "So whenever this component is created in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.86,
          "end": 17.55,
          "en": "Now, you can use the constructor for tasks like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.55,
          "end": 19.44,
          "en": "It's not wrong,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.44,
          "end": 21.66,
          "en": "but it's typically recommended",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.66,
          "end": 25.41,
          "en": "that you use a different component method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.41,
          "end": 29.13,
          "en": "because all those Angular Components go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.13,
          "end": 33.21,
          "en": "through a component life cycle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.21,
          "end": 37.47,
          "en": "and that simply means that when Angular instantiates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.47,
          "end": 39.51,
          "en": "and renders that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.51,
          "end": 43.29,
          "en": "and when it then checks it for changes in the future,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.29,
          "end": 48.21,
          "en": "certain lifecycle hooks are triggered by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.21,
          "end": 51.78,
          "en": "Certain methods you can add to your component class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.78,
          "end": 55.02,
          "en": "to run code at certain points in time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.02,
          "end": 57.243,
          "en": "of this component's lifecycle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.5,
          "end": 60.57,
          "en": "We already solved the constructor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.57,
          "end": 64.56,
          "en": "but therefore example also is an ngOnInit method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.56,
          "end": 66.376,
          "en": "you can add to a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.376,
          "end": 69.33,
          "en": "because as you learn in the official docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.33,
          "end": 72.29599999999999,
          "en": "and a link to this article is attached,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.29599999999999,
          "end": 74.736,
          "en": "this ngOnInit method will be executed by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.736,
          "end": 79.736,
          "en": "whenever Angular has initialized this component's inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.67,
          "end": 83.28,
          "en": "So whenever it essentially is done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.28,
          "end": 85.053,
          "en": "initializing this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.43,
          "end": 88.71000000000001,
          "en": "There also are some other hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.71000000000001,
          "end": 90.101,
          "en": "and I'll say right away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.101,
          "end": 93.66,
          "en": "that you typically don't need all of them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.66,
          "end": 97.25999999999999,
          "en": "Some of them are for pretty niche cases,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.25999999999999,
          "end": 99.18,
          "en": "but I'll get back to them later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.18,
          "end": 102.843,
          "en": "For the moment it's this ngOnInit hook I'm interested in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.1,
          "end": 107.85,
          "en": "To get Angular to execute it, all you have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.85,
          "end": 111.53999999999999,
          "en": "to do is go to your component where you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.53999999999999,
          "end": 115.551,
          "en": "to do something at that point in the component lifecycle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.551,
          "end": 120.551,
          "en": "and you add the ngOnInit method to that component class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.01,
          "end": 124.95,
          "en": "That's all. Now Angular will execute it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.95,
          "end": 126.57300000000001,
          "en": "It only needs to be there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.74,
          "end": 130.89,
          "en": "So now we can grab that code from the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.89,
          "end": 133.473,
          "en": "and instead execute it in ngOnInit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.87,
          "end": 138.975,
          "en": "Now, even though it did work in the constructor without",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.975,
          "end": 142.02,
          "en": "problems, and even though it wouldn't be wrong",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.02,
          "end": 144.06,
          "en": "for simple use cases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.06,
          "end": 145.82999999999998,
          "en": "and applications like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.82999999999998,
          "end": 150.18,
          "en": "you should actually prefer using ngOnInit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.18,
          "end": 154.41,
          "en": "for initialization work like setting up this interval,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.41,
          "end": 158.76,
          "en": "it is considered a good practice in Angular applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.76,
          "end": 161.28,
          "en": "to keep your constructor lean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.28,
          "end": 165.32999999999998,
          "en": "and only do basic class initialization",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.32999999999998,
          "end": 166.56,
          "en": "work in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.56,
          "end": 170.34,
          "en": "So if you wanna assign some initial class property values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.34,
          "end": 172.8,
          "en": "or things like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.8,
          "end": 176.1,
          "en": "Anything else, especially more complex tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.1,
          "end": 178.451,
          "en": "like sending HTTP requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.451,
          "end": 180.72,
          "en": "which we'll do later in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.72,
          "end": 183.36,
          "en": "should not go into the constructor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183.36,
          "end": 185.643,
          "en": "but instead into ngOnInit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 186.624,
          "end": 189.57,
          "en": "In addition, as you can also see in the official",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.57,
          "end": 193.77,
          "en": "documentation, one difference between the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.77,
          "end": 198.32999999999998,
          "en": "and ngOnInit also is that in ngOnInit in it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 198.32999999999998,
          "end": 202.11,
          "en": "Angular is done initializing the component inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.11,
          "end": 205.14,
          "en": "So if your component receives any input values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.14,
          "end": 207.21,
          "en": "those values will be initialized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207.21,
          "end": 210.84,
          "en": "and will be available in ngOnInit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.84,
          "end": 214.11,
          "en": "whereas that is not the case in the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 214.11,
          "end": 217.86,
          "en": "So that might be another reason for using ngOnInit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 217.86,
          "end": 219.84,
          "en": "But as mentioned in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 219.84,
          "end": 223.95,
          "en": "you should simply prefer it over the constructor to follow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.95,
          "end": 226.173,
          "en": "that recommended best practice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 227.22,
          "end": 231.18,
          "en": "With that change made, if you save that, you'll see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 231.18,
          "end": 235.44,
          "en": "that if you reload, this application still works the same it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 235.44,
          "end": 239.253,
          "en": "did before, eventually the server status will change.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
